{"title":"2012 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part A","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rowan is given a square grid whose side length is an odd integer. The square is then divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> squares,. Rowan shades each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square along the two diagonals and does not shade any of the remaining squares. For example, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> grid is shown in which Rowan has shaded the squares along the diagonals.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rowan is given a square grid that is 7 by 7. How many by 1 squares does he shade?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can draw a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4f93df0d5696a7a30826c6a7c604d1352c6198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 7$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> square grid and then shade the squares along the diagonals:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Counting, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e40bc2b9bcef49b195e9be1e88febb6eff5fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> squares are shaded.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the number of shaded squares for a square grid is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f5a5ded7724c11e58ef212dc3e8549071890a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a whole number representing the number of rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a5c5d3772d6b4c76f955e254c12563ca27b9ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> because there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> squares for each diagonal, except the center square is repeated twice. \n</p><p>Thus, Rowan shades <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d95a27f751979bb42d983e7ea282704341b05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 7 - 1 = 14 - 1 = \\boxed{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"201\" height=\"25\" /> squares.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055258\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 70/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1730/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2272/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.167      1 -total\n 96.04%   13.606      1 2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n 42.77%    6.059      2 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37083:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055258 and revision id 286388. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}